      "title": "WHO Digital Transformation Handbook",
      "description": "The register of WHO's Digital Transformation Handbooks (DTHs) — the guidance publications that take one area of a health system from paper to digital within the DIIG process: the order of digitization, digitalization and digital transformation, what a registry is against a register, what master data excludes, and how the draft DPI-H Reference Architecture names its own layers. Derived rule by rule from the three DTHs and the draft Reference Architecture ingested in smart-base/library; every rule cites the section it was read from, and a rule resting on the DRAFT says so.",
